course: dictionary
lesson: 4209
title: Words from around the world
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words name things you may never have seen. You can work out a lot from the words around them. «Every corner of the world built its own instruments from what was at hand: gourds, termite-hollowed branches, bamboo, old oil drums.» This list is full of things people use to make instruments, so a gourd is probably something that can be shaped into one.
explain: «The kora is a West African instrument with 21 strings, made from a large gourd covered in skin.» The gourd is what the kora is made from, and it has skin stretched over it, like a drum. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence to check it still makes sense.
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. A gourd can be a fruit, a bottle or a rattle, and the clues in the sentence tell you which one. Out of your gourd is a slang phrase from America meaning crazy or silly. It has nothing to do with fruit at all.
fact: A gourd is a large fruit with a hard skin, related to pumpkins and melons.
fact: Dried gourds can be hollowed out and used as containers, bottles or bowls.
fact: A gourd can also be a rattle, a musical instrument that you shake to make a sound.
fact: The kora is a West African instrument with 21 strings, made from a large gourd covered in skin.
fact: Griots are musicians who keep history alive through song.
fact: Out of your gourd is US slang meaning crazy or silly.
exercise: «The kora is a West African instrument with 21 strings, made from a large gourd covered in skin.» What is the kora made from? | Pumpkin seeds and string | *A large gourd covered in skin | Metal oil drums | Bamboo cut into thin sticks
exercise: Find and copy one word from «Every corner of the world built its own instruments from what was at hand: gourds, termite-hollowed branches, bamboo, old oil drums.» that names something you could use to make an instrument. | *gourds | hand | corner | world
exercise: Tom says, «Jake is out of his gourd!» What does Tom mean? | *Jake is acting crazy or silly | Jake has grown a giant pumpkin | Jake is very thirsty | Jake has found a dried gourd
test: A dried gourd is often hollowed out. What does hollowed out mean? | Cut into very small pieces | Filled with seeds and water | *Emptied on the inside | Painted bright orange
test: Which phrase means a bottle made from a dried gourd? | a gourd fruit with a hard skin | *a water gourd | out of your gourd | a gourd rattle
exam: Using the clues in «made from a large gourd covered in skin», what kind of thing is a gourd here? | A musician who plays the kora | A tiny seed | A type of string | *A large, hollow shape used as the body of an instrument
